{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Strong negative bias: model systematically underprices the true path by ~+2 to +5 EUR most days; apply an upward level shift (e.g., add +3 EUR baseline, increasing to +4–5 EUR when trend is strongly up).",
    "Trend/lag error in rallies: during persistent uptrends the model lags and mean-reverts too early; increase trend-following weight so multi-day rises propagate forward (especially days 5–25 of the horizon).",
    "Horizon-dependent drift: underprediction grows with forecast horizon (errors widen after ~day 7–10); use a horizon ramp correction (small uplift near-term, larger uplift mid/long-term).",
    "Volatility compression: forecast range is too narrow versus outcomes (misses highs); expand amplitude by scaling deviations from the forecast mean upward (e.g., multiply deviations by ~1.2–1.4 in strong-trend regimes).",
    "Post-dip rebound underestimation: after local lows in history, the model expects continued softness but true series rebounds strongly; add a rebound premium when recent 5–10 day momentum turns positive from a low base."
  ]
}
